\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation and group the terms on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}(0)-4t(\\alpha )+6(\\alpha t+\\beta ) & =2t+6 \\\\ (-4\\alpha +6\\alpha )t+6\\beta  & =2t+6 \\\\ 2\\alpha t+6\\beta  & =2t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,t) \\\\ 6\\beta =6\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha = 1$ and $\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution $y_p(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny_p(t) = t + 1.\n$$" 13194139535880 true] [17592186151897 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$x^2 y'' + xy' - y = 3x^2, \\quad x>0$." 13194139535880 false] [17592186151897 1100 "Find the general solution to the equation \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071621/assets/5dec2a9790065a32f95712885a67f7893f3f323f0c342bc19848686f1680ad47.png)" 13194139535880 true] [17592186151897 1145 "First, we need to find the complementary function ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071621/assets/3d25b04f73a69c37a53b7aa96c2435aafafad5068285766fc814009b9256b713.png) which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071621/assets/1cbb2d785492c25c8fe56009cf52999f8d95ad1894b2639b40b76dc0ba5d996f.png)\n\nLet ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071621/assets/e9f6c9cb15008e44ba966d9e924910ca3c727c4b5755675eb5aa2ca56ac7d1ba.png) Differentiating ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14071621/assets/bb8d120334b114f86a714