tion to the equation \n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-3t{y}^{′}-5y=8{t}^{2},\\,t>0.\n$$" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372140 1113 #uuid "cf01ae1c-fdd1-5411-bb0e-3e2065f6bccf" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372140 1145 "First, we need to find the complimentary function ${y}_{c}(t)$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-3t{y}^{′}-5y=0.\n$$\n\nLet $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-3t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}-5{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-3\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }-5{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda -5] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-3\\lambda -5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -5 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =-1$ and $\\lambda =5.$ Thus, the complimentary function ${y}_{c}(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(t)=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is proportional to ${t}^{2}.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is of the form \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\alpha {t}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is the constant that is to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}t}=2\\alpha t,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{t}^{2}}=2\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation and group the terms on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}(2\\alpha )-3t(2\\alpha t)-5(\\alpha {t}^{2}) & =8{t}^{2} \\\\ (2\\alpha -6\\alpha -5\\alpha ){t}^{2} & =8{t}^{2} \\\\ -9\\alpha {t}^{2} & =8{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get $\\alpha =-\\frac{8}{9}.$\n\nHence, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{8{t}^{2}}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & ={y}_{c}(t)+{y}_{p}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}-\\frac{8{t}^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372142 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372143 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372144 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372145 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186372146 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1041 "selection" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1104 #edb/ref 17592186372143 13194139535880 true] [17592186372141 1110 #uuid "aa7fc19e-3a5f-5c3c-82a2-f08de8c4ffdd" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372142 1034 "y(t)={c}_{1}t+\\frac{{c}_{2}}{{t}^{5}}-\\frac{8{t}^{2}}{9}" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535880 true] [17592186372142 1111 #uuid "0335a7cd-a610-576d-ac36-323e67ebbb5c" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372143 1034 "y(t)=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}-\\frac{8{t}^{2}}{9}" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535880 true] [17592186372143 1111 #uuid "cebb03ac-2f9a-591f-a846-b1e196246005" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372144 1034 "y(t)=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{9}" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535880 true] [17592186372144 1111 #uuid "16c16e2e-7cfd-5530-b8ab-70e05021c24b" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372145 1034 "y(t)=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{t}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}-8{t}^{2}" 13194139535880 true] [17592186372145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535880 true] [17592186372145 1111 #uuid "ddd9efa7-6cda-5aa4-a9f5-fab03de9efe1" 1319413953